    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">This novel brings to life the rich history and traditions of the Bharath people, a group whose presence in Tamil literature is often overlooked. Set in a small fishing village, the story spans over fifty years, exploring the lives, beliefs, and struggles of its inhabitants through the lens of three generations. The narrative delves into the profound relationship between the ocean and its people, reflecting on themes of love, sacrifice, and the passage of time. By vividly depicting the ebb and flow of life, the novel captures the essence of human resilience and the enduring spirit of its characters, making it a notable addition to Tamil literary achievements.</marc:subfield>
